        "body": "Gain 2, Work 2, Harm 2\nCase: normal use - a reviewed stacked child's PR check finishes while its parent remains unmerged.\nThis refusal deliberately produces a failed `forge-pr-check` status. However, `nextstep._item_readiness()` maps that failure to `checks failed` (src/forge/nextstep.py:867-868), while the stacked-status logic recognizes a clean review only for `ready` or `waiting for checks` (lines 639-643). Consequently, `forge next` and the board describe the reviewed child as still building and direct users back to closing it instead of merging its parent. Repeating close cannot clear this intentional failure. Update the existing status consumer to distinguish the expected stacking refusal from actual failed checks; the changed status tests currently supply only successful or pending checks.",
